<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mir Jumla II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1591">1591</a>–<a href="/years/1663">1663</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Mir Muhammad Said Ardestani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mir Jumla II was a Persian-born merchant, general and statesman who served the Golconda Sultanate and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>. Made governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a>, he invaded Cooch Behar and the Ahom kingdom in 1661–1663, occupied the Ahom capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garhgaon">Garhgaon</a> and imposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ghilajharighat">Treaty of Ghilajharighat</a>, but his army was ruined by disease and floods and he died on the return march in 1663.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mir-jumla-ii.jpg" alt="Mir Jumla II" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mir_Jumla_-_peinture_-_btv1b52505099t.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
